56.jpg","art":"/data/forever/img/dungeons/naxxramas/art.jpg"},"chests":[],"descriptionEn":"Naxxramas was a 40-man raid added in patch 1.11. Originally floating above the Eastern Plaguelands, it was a massive necropolis and had the honor of serving as the seat of one of the Lich King's most powerful officers, the lich Kel'Thuzad. The raid was regarded as the most difficult before the release of The Burning Crusade, and required 40 well-equipped (preferably Tier 2 or Tier 2.5 armor) players.","entrance":{"x":39.0,"y":25.0,"zoneName":"Eastern Plaguelands","zoneId":139,"zoneMapId":139,"zoneMap":"/data/forever/img/zones/139.jpg"}}